# git-identity: directory → profile map  (used by gitclone and gitinit)
#
# One rule per line, whitespace-separated:
#
#   <path-glob>   <alias>   <owner>
#
#   path-glob  matched against $PWD (gitclone) or the target dir (gitinit).
#              ~ expands to $HOME. ** crosses slashes.
#   alias      identity alias from `identities`.
#   owner      GitHub org/user used to build remote URLs in gitinit.
#
# Evaluated top-to-bottom; FIRST match wins. Put specific rules above the
# catch-all. Lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# Example (replace with your real project tree):
#   ~/Projects/clientA/**     work       clientA-org
#   ~/Projects/personal/**    personal   my-gh-user
#   ~/Projects/**             work       my-default-owner
